{title: Take Time to Be Holy}
{artist: William D. Longstaff / George C. Stebbins}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: F}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 6/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnal for Worship & Celebration (Nashville, Tennessee: Word Music, 1986), # 441)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Take time to be holy,
[F]Speak oft with thy Lord;
[F]Abide in Him always,
[C7]And feed on His Word.
[C7]Make friends of God’s [F]children,
[C7]Help those who are [F]weak,
[F]Forgetting in [Bb]nothing
[F]His blessing to seek.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Take time to be holy,
[F]The world rushes on;
[F]Spend much time in secret,
[C7]With Jesus alone.
[C7]By looking to [F]Jesus,
[C7]Like Him thou shalt [F]be;
[F]Thy friends in thy [Bb]conduct
[F]His likeness shall see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Take time to be holy,
[F]Let Him be thy guide;
[F]And run not before Him,
[C7]Whatever betide.
[C7]In joy or in [F]sorrow,
[C7]Still follow the [F]Lord,
[F]And, looking to [Bb]Jesus,
[F]Still trust in His Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Take time to be holy,
[F]Be calm in thy soul,
[F]Each thought and each motive
[C7]Beneath His control.
[C7]Thus led by His [F]Spirit
[C7]To fountains of [F]love,
[F]Thou soon shalt be [Bb]fitted
[F]For service above.
{end_of_verse}
